    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The main arguments in these antitrust cases generally center on the power and dominance of big tech like Google and Amazon.\n\nProponents of the investigations argue that these \"gatekeepers\" engage in anti-competitive behavior, using their massive market power to stifle smaller rivals and control the digital landscape unfairly.\n\nOpponents argue that these powerful companies are simply benefiting from superior innovation, strong consumer choices, and are necessary for the digital ecosystem to function effectively.\n\nThe debate ultimately revolves around whether these dominant market positions are the result of superior competition or anti-competitive tactics that harm the public and competition.",
